From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:39:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] radv: fix a memory leak when allocating a pool entry
 failed

When radv_descriptor_set_create() fails, it breaks the loop in
radv_AllocateDescriptorSets() and the entry i isn't set, so nothing is
freed.

Fixes: 849d41dbf83 ("radv: implement a new descriptor sets allocator")
Signed-off-by: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45169>
(cherry picked from commit a86c98dae8ac5a14841e1f64ddb25153af590282)

Io: from Mesa main (Valve picked it for steamos-26.05), not in 26.2.5
yet; the .pick_status.json part left out.
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c
index 00289261a11..1a004757fc2 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_set.c
@@ -460,8 +460,15 @@ radv_descriptor_set_create(struct radv_device *device, struct radv_descriptor_po
    set->header.size = align(layout_size, 32);
 
    result = radv_alloc_descriptor_pool_entry(device, pool, set);
-   if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
+   if (result != VK_SUCCESS) {
+      vk_object_base_finish(&set->header.base);
+      if (pool->host_memory_base) {
+         pool->host_memory_ptr -= mem_size;
+      } else {
+         vk_free2(&device->vk.alloc, NULL, set);
+      }
       return result;
+   }
 
    if (layout->has_immutable_samplers) {
       for (unsigned i = 0; i < layout->binding_count; ++i) {
